        <h3 id="sec-6-1">
          6.1 <code>WireUint</code> (<code>WireType = 0</code>) &amp; <code>WireSint</code> (
          <code>WireType = 12</code>)
        </h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireUint</code> (<code>0</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Encodes an unsigned integer (<code>uint32</code>, <code>uint64</code>, <code>enum</code>
            ) as a single Prefix-Varint immediately after the tag.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireSint</code> (<code>12</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Encodes a signed integer (<code>int32</code>, <code>int64</code>, <code>sint32</code>,{' '}
            <code>sint64</code>) mapped via ZigZag (<code>EncodeZigZag(n)</code>) as a single
            Prefix-Varint immediately after the tag.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>
            Example 1: Field <code>#1</code> (<code>asn = 64512</code>, <code>WireUint = 0</code>):
          </strong>
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            Tag: <code>(1 &lt;&lt; 4) | 0 = 16</code> &rarr; 1-byte Prefix-Varint{' '}
            <code>(16 &lt;&lt; 1) | 1 = 0x21</code>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Value: <code>64512</code> (<code>&gt; 16383</code>, 4-byte Prefix-Varint{' '}
            <code>TZCNT = 2</code>): <code>(64512 &lt;&lt; 3) | 4 = 0x0007E004</code> &rarr;
            little-endian <code>04 e0 07 00</code>.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <pre><code><span class="text-acid font-bold">21</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">04 e0 07 00</span>
<span class="text-acid">^^</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">^^^^^^^^^^^</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span> <span class="text-paper/85">Value = 64512 (LE32: 0x0007E004 &gt;&gt; 3)</span></code></pre>

        <p>
          <strong>
            Example 2: Field <code>#5</code> (<code>rssi_dbm = -62</code>,{' '}
            <code>WireSint = 12</code>):
          </strong>
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            Tag: <code>(5 &lt;&lt; 4) | 12 = 92</code> &rarr; 1-byte Prefix-Varint{' '}
            <code>(92 &lt;&lt; 1) | 1 = 185 = 0xB9</code>.
          </li>
          <li>
            ZigZag of <code>-62</code>: <code>EncodeZigZag(-62) = 123</code> &rarr; 1-byte
            Prefix-Varint <code>(123 &lt;&lt; 1) | 1 = 247 = 0xF7</code>.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <pre><code><span class="text-acid font-bold">b9</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">f7</span>
<span class="text-acid">^^</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">^^</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span> <span class="text-paper/85">Value = -62 (ZigZag 123 -&gt; DecodeZigZag(0xF7 &gt;&gt; 1) = -62)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-2">
          6.2 <code>WireBoolFalse</code> (<code>WireType = 1</code>) &amp; <code>WireBoolTrue</code>{' '}
          (<code>WireType = 2</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Boolean values consume <strong>0 payload bytes</strong> after the tag; the boolean state
          is encoded directly in the 4-bit <code>WireType</code>.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-acid font-bold">65</span>
<span class="text-acid">^^</span>
<span class="text-paper/85">Field #3, WireBoolTrue (true) -- (if false, tag is 0x63)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-3">
          6.3 <code>WireString</code> (<code>WireType = 3</code>) &amp; <code>WireBytes</code> (
          <code>WireType = 4</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Followed by <code>[ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)]</code> and <code>[ByteLen raw bytes]</code>.
          Strings are UTF-8 encoded without a trailing NUL terminator.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-acid font-bold">47</span>  <span class="text-[#FFAB70] font-bold">09</span>  <span class="text-[#A5D6FF]">72 74 72 31</span>
<span class="text-acid">^^</span>  <span class="text-[#FFAB70]">^^</span>  <span class="text-[#A5D6FF]">^^^^^^^^^^^</span>
<span class="text-acid">Tag</span> <span class="text-[#FFAB70]">Len</span> <span class="text-paper/85">"rtr1" (Field #2, ByteLen = 4)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-4">
          6.4 <code>WireSubMsg</code> (<code>WireType = 5</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Encodes a nested message as <code>[ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)][Inner Message Bytes]</code>.
          Encoders typically emit <code>ByteLen</code> as a 2-byte Prefix-Varint (
          <code>TZCNT = 1</code>) via single-pass backpatching, though decoders MUST accept any
          valid Prefix-Varint width for <code>ByteLen</code>.
        </p>
        <pre><code><span class="text-paper/65">Inner Sub-Message (7 bytes):</span>
  Offset 0x00: <span class="text-acid font-bold">67</span> <span class="text-[#FFAB70]">07</span> <span class="text-[#A5D6FF]">46 52 41</span>   <span class="text-paper/65">-&gt; Inner Field #3 (WireString): tag=0x67, len=3 (0x07), "FRA"</span>
  Offset 0x05: <span class="text-acid font-bold">81</span> <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">55</span>            <span class="text-paper/65">-&gt; Inner Field #4 (WireUint):   tag=0x81, val=42 (0x55 = 42&lt;&lt;1|1)</span>

<span class="text-paper/65">Outer Field #9 Wrapping (2B Tag + 2B Overlong ByteLen + 7B Inner Message = 11 bytes):</span>
  <span class="text-acid font-bold">56 02</span>  <span class="text-[#FFAB70] font-bold">1e 00</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">67 07 46 52 41 81 55</span>
  <span class="text-acid">^^^^^</span>  <span class="text-[#FFAB70]">^^^^^</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^</span>
  <span class="text-acid">Tag#9</span>  <span class="text-[#FFAB70]">Len=7</span>  <span class="text-paper/85">Inner Sub-Message (7 bytes)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-5">
          6.5 <code>WireStringArr</code> (<code>WireType = 6</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Encodes a list of length-prefixed strings or byte slices (<code>repeated string</code> or{' '}
          <code>repeated bytes</code>) with an outer <code>ByteLen</code> prefix so decoders and
          skippers can jump over the entire array in a single <code>O(1)</code> addition without
          walking individual elements:
        </p>
        <pre><code>+-----+---------------------------+----------------------------+-------------------------------+
| Tag | ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)   | ElemCount (Prefix-Varint)  | [StrLen (Varint)][UTF-8]...   |
+-----+---------------------------+----------------------------+-------------------------------+
                                  |&lt;---------------------- ByteLen bytes ---------------------&gt;|

Example: Field #7 (tags = ["a", "bc"]):
  ed  1a 00  05   03 61   05 62 63
  ^^  ^^^^^  ^^^  ^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^
  Tag Len=6  N=2  "a"     "bc"</code></pre>
        <p>
          Sharing <code>WireStringArr</code> (<code>6</code>) between <code>repeated string</code>{' '}
          and <code>repeated bytes</code> keeps all 16 wire types (<code>0..15</code>) packed into 4
          bits; schema-aware decoders know the target slice type (<code>[]string</code> vs.{' '}
          <code>[][]byte</code>), while schema-less text/JSON formatters can check{' '}
          <code>utf8.Valid(elem)</code> when rendering elements.
        </p>

        <h3 id="sec-6-6">
          6.6 <code>WireUintArr</code> (<code>WireType = 7</code>) &amp; <code>WireSintArr</code> (
          <code>WireType = 13</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Encodes a packed array of unsigned (<code>WireUintArr</code>) or ZigZag-encoded signed (
          <code>WireSintArr</code>) integers with an outer byte-length prefix so decoders and
          skippers can jump over the entire array in a single addition without decoding individual
          varints, while preserving signedness in schema-less decoding (<code>DecodeBlind</code>):
        </p>
        <pre><code>+-----+---------------------------+----------------------------+--------------------------+
| Tag | ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)   | ElemCount (Prefix-Varint)  | Elem_0 ... Elem_N-1      |
+-----+---------------------------+----------------------------+--------------------------+
                                  |&lt;------------------- ByteLen bytes -------------------&gt;|

Example: Field #8 (prefixes = [10, 300]):
  1e 02  12 00  05   15  b2 04
  ^^^^^  ^^^^^  ^^^  ^^  ^^^^^
  Tag#8  Len=4  N=2  10  300</code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-7">
          6.7 <code>WireSubMsgArr</code> (<code>WireType = 8</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Encodes <code>repeated message</code> as a single contiguous container with an outer{' '}
          <code>ByteLen</code> prefix followed by length-prefixed sub-message elements:
        </p>
        <pre><code>+-----+---------+-----------------------------+-----+-----------------------------------+
| Tag | ByteLen | ElemLen_0 (Varint) | Elem_0 | ... | ElemLen_&#123;N-1&#125; (Varint) | Elem_N-1 |
+-----+---------+-----------------------------+-----+-----------------------------------+
                |&lt;--------------------------- ByteLen bytes ---------------------------&gt;|</code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <code>ByteLen &gt;= 0</code>. If <code>ByteLen == 0</code>, the array contains{' '}
            <code>0</code> elements.
          </li>
          <li>
            Each element <code>i</code> is preceded by its byte length <code>ElemLen_i</code>{' '}
            encoded as a Prefix-Varint, followed by <code>ElemLen_i</code> bytes of the element's
            OmniBuf message.
          </li>
          <li>
            The sum of all <code>(len(ElemLen_i) + ElemLen_i)</code> across all elements MUST equal{' '}
            <code>ByteLen</code> exactly.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-6-8">
          6.8 <code>WireMap</code> (<code>WireType = 9</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Encodes any Protobuf <code>map&lt;K, V&gt;</code> as a length-prefixed container with a
          1-byte <code>MapType</code> header followed by <code>EntryCount</code> key-value pairs:
        </p>
        <pre><code>+-----+---------+-------------------------------+----------------------------+-------------------+
| Tag | ByteLen | MapType (KeyWT&lt;&lt;4 | ValWT)    | EntryCount (Prefix-Varint) | [Key][Value]...   |
+-----+---------+-------------------------------+----------------------------+-------------------+
                |&lt;-------------------------------- ByteLen bytes -------------------------------&gt;|</code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              1-Byte <code>MapType</code> Header:
            </strong>{' '}
            Immediately after <code>ByteLen</code>, a single byte encodes{' '}
            <code>(KeyWireType &lt;&lt; 4) | ValWireType</code>:
            <ul>
              <li>
                <code>KeyWireType</code>: <code>WireUint</code> (<code>0</code>, for{' '}
                <code>uint32/uint64/bool</code>), <code>WireString</code> (<code>3</code>, for{' '}
                <code>string</code>), <code>WireFixed32</code> (<code>10</code>),{' '}
                <code>WireFixed64</code> (<code>11</code>), or <code>WireSint</code> (
                <code>12</code>, for <code>int32/int64/sint32/sint64</code>).
              </li>
              <li>
                <code>ValWireType</code>: <code>WireUint</code> (<code>0</code>, for{' '}
                <code>uint32/uint64/enum/bool</code>), <code>WireString</code> (<code>3</code>),{' '}
                <code>WireBytes</code> (<code>4</code>), <code>WireSubMsg</code> (<code>5</code>),{' '}
                <code>WireFixed32</code> (<code>10</code>), <code>WireFixed64</code> (
                <code>11</code>), or <code>WireSint</code> (<code>12</code>).
              </li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              Minimum Container Length (<code>ByteLen &gt;= 2</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Every <code>WireMap</code> container includes the 1-byte <code>MapType</code> header
            followed by <code>EntryCount</code> (Prefix-Varint, at least 1 byte), so{' '}
            <code>ByteLen</code> MUST be <code>&gt;= 2</code> (an empty map with{' '}
            <code>EntryCount = 0</code> has <code>ByteLen = 2</code>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Untagged Self-Framing Entries:</strong> Each of the <code>EntryCount</code>{' '}
            entries consists of the untagged payload of <code>KeyWireType</code> followed
            immediately by the untagged payload of <code>ValWireType</code> (for example, when{' '}
            <code>ValWireType</code> is <code>WireSubMsg</code> (<code>5</code>), the value payload
            is <code>[ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)][Inner Message Bytes]</code>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Unordered Keys &amp; "Last Write Wins":</strong> Entries may appear in any key
            order, allowing encoders to iterate native hash maps directly in <code>O(N)</code> time
            with zero sorting or temporary slice allocations. If a key appears multiple times
            (within a container or across concatenated messages), the last occurrence wins.
          </li>
          <li>
            The end of the last entry (<code>Entry_&#123;EntryCount-1&#125;</code>) MUST align
            exactly with <code>ByteLen</code>.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-6-9">
          6.9 <code>WireFixed32</code> (<code>WireType = 10</code>) &amp; <code>WireFixed64</code> (
          <code>WireType = 11</code>)
        </h3>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireFixed32</code> (<code>10</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Followed by exactly <strong>4 bytes</strong> in little-endian order (<code>uint32</code>
            , <code>int32</code>, or IEEE-754 binary32 <code>float32</code>).
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>WireFixed64</code> (<code>11</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Followed by exactly <strong>8 bytes</strong> in little-endian order (<code>uint64</code>
            , <code>int64</code>, or IEEE-754 binary64 <code>float64</code>).
          </li>
        </ul>
        <pre><code>Example: Field #6 (cpu_load = 0.5 as float64):
  <span class="text-acid font-bold">d7</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">00 00 00 00 00 00 e0 3f</span>
  <span class="text-acid">^^</span>  <span class="text-[#79C0FF]">^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^</span>
  <span class="text-acid">Tag</span> <span class="text-paper/85">IEEE-754 0.5 (LE64)</span></code></pre>

        <h3 id="sec-6-10">
          6.10 <code>WireFixedArr</code> (<code>WireType = 14</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Encodes a packed array of fixed-width 32-bit or 64-bit little-endian elements with an
          outer <code>ByteLen</code> prefix followed by a 1-byte <code>ElemType</code> header:
        </p>
        <pre><code>+-----+---------+-------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| Tag | ByteLen | ElemType (1B: WireFixed32=10 or 11) | Little-Endian Elements...    |
+-----+---------+-------------------------------------+------------------------------+
                |&lt;-------------------------- ByteLen bytes -------------------------&gt;|</code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>ByteLen &gt;= 1</code>:
            </strong>{' '}
            Every <code>WireFixedArr</code> container includes the 1-byte <code>ElemType</code>{' '}
            header, so <code>ByteLen</code> MUST be <code>&gt;= 1</code>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>ElemType = WireFixed32</code> (<code>10</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Followed by <code>(ByteLen - 1) / 4</code> little-endian 4-byte elements (
            <code>repeated float</code>, <code>repeated fixed32</code>,{' '}
            <code>repeated sfixed32</code>). <code>(ByteLen - 1)</code> MUST be a multiple of{' '}
            <code>4</code>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>ElemType = WireFixed64</code> (<code>11</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Followed by <code>(ByteLen - 1) / 8</code> little-endian 8-byte elements (
            <code>repeated double</code>, <code>repeated fixed64</code>,{' '}
            <code>repeated sfixed64</code>). <code>(ByteLen - 1)</code> MUST be a multiple of{' '}
            <code>8</code>.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-6-11">
          6.11 <code>WireExtended</code> (<code>WireType = 15</code>)
        </h3>
        <p>
          Reserves <code>WireType = 15</code> as a forward-compatible, length-prefixed extension
          escape hatch capable of expressing up to 256 extended wire types while remaining skippable
          in <code>O(1)</code> time by existing decoders:
        </p>
        <pre><code>+-----+---------------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------------------+
| Tag | ByteLen (Prefix-Varint)   | ExtType (1B: 0..255)  | ExtPayload (ByteLen - 1 bytes)    |
+-----+---------------------------+-----------------------+-----------------------------------+
                                  |&lt;--------------------- ByteLen bytes ---------------------&gt;|</code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>ByteLen &gt;= 1</code>:
            </strong>{' '}
            Every <code>WireExtended</code> container starts with <code>ByteLen</code> followed by a
            1-byte extended type identifier <code>ExtType</code> (<code>0..255</code>) and{' '}
            <code>ByteLen - 1</code> bytes of extended payload.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              <code>O(1)</code> Forward-Compatible Skipping:
            </strong>{' '}
            Because <code>WireExtended</code> begins with <code>ByteLen</code> just like every other
            variable-length container, <code>SkipValue</code> skips any unknown future{' '}
            <code>WireExtended</code> field in a single arithmetic jump (
            <code>pos + tn + byteLen</code>) without needing to understand <code>ExtType</code>.
          </li>
          <li>
            In Version 1.0, no <code>ExtType</code> values are assigned; schema-less decoders (
            <code>DecodeBlind</code>) MUST reject unrecognized <code>ExtType</code> values, while
            schema-aware decoders MUST skip unknown fields carrying <code>WireExtended</code>.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <!-- SECTION 7 -->
        <h2 id="sec-7">
          7. Branchless <code>TZCNT</code> Header-Hop Field Lookup (<code>LocateField</code>)
        </h2>
        <p>
          In Protocol Buffers, skipping a preceding <code>varint</code> field requires a
          byte-by-byte continuation-bit loop. In OmniBuf, every scalar width is determined from{' '}
          <code>b[0]</code> via <code>TZCNT</code>, booleans are <code>0</code> bytes after the tag,
          and every container starts with <code>ByteLen</code>, enabling an <strong>O(1)</strong>{' '}
          arithmetic jump per field without parsing inside containers:
        </p>
        <Code code={locateFieldGoCode} lang="go" theme="github-dark" />

        <!-- SECTION 8 -->
        <h2 id="sec-8">
          8. Optional Inline Schema (<code>Field #0</code>, <code>omnibuf.v1.SchemaMeta</code>)
        </h2>
        <p>
          When self-describing mode is enabled,{' '}
          <strong>
            Field <code>#0</code>
          </strong>{' '}
          (<code>Tag = 0x0B</code>, <code>WireSubMsg = 5</code>) is written at byte <code>0</code>{' '}
          of the root message (or at the beginning of a nested sub-message or concatenated message
          segment) as a regular OmniBuf sub-message encoding <code>omnibuf.v1.SchemaMeta</code>.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Zero-Cost Skipping for Schema-Aware Decoders:</strong> Because{' '}
            <code>Field #0</code> is a standard <code>WireSubMsg</code> (<code>5</code>) starting
            with <code>ByteLen</code>, a schema-aware decoder sees tag <code>0x0B</code>, reads{' '}
            <code>ByteLen</code>, and jumps over the entire metadata block in a single{' '}
            <code>O(1)</code> addition.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Dogfooding &amp; Extensibility:</strong> Because <code>Field #0</code> is
            defined by its own <code>.proto</code> schema (<code>schemas/meta.proto</code>), future
            optional metadata fields (such as schema hashes or enum value tables) can be added to{' '}
            <code>SchemaMeta</code> without changing the OmniBuf wire version.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-8-1">
          8.1 <code>omnibuf.v1.SchemaMeta</code> Definition (<code>meta.proto</code>)
        </h3>
        <Code code={sec8MetaProtoCode} lang="protobuf" theme="github-dark" />
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              Keyed by <code>FieldNumber</code> (<code>map&lt;uint32, string&gt; fields = 2</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Each entry in <code>fields</code> maps a <code>FieldNumber</code> (1B{' '}
            <code>WireUint</code> varint for fields <code>1..127</code>) to its{' '}
            <code>FieldName</code> (<code>WireString</code>). Unlike positional string lists, keying
            by <code>FieldNumber</code> turns <code>SchemaMeta</code> into a reusable type
            descriptor that works across every instance of a message regardless of which optional
            fields are present or omitted.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>
              Hoisted Child Schemas (<code>map&lt;uint32, SchemaMeta&gt; children = 3</code>):
            </strong>{' '}
            Maps a parent field number (for a nested <code>WireSubMsg</code>, a{' '}
            <code>WireSubMsgArr</code> repeated sub-message array, or a <code>WireMap</code>{' '}
            sub-message value) to its child <code>SchemaMeta</code>.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-8-2">
          8.2 Single Message Wire Encoding with <code>Field #0</code>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Consider a <code>Location</code> message (<code>city = "FRA"</code> at Field{' '}
          <code>#3</code>, <code>rack = 42</code> at Field <code>#4</code>) encoded with{' '}
          <code>Field #0</code> (<code>type_name = "Location"</code>,{' '}
          <code>fields = &#123;3: "city", 4: "rack"&#125;</code>):
