        <h3 id="sec-8-3">
          8.3 <code>repeated message</code> (<code>WireSubMsgArr</code>) Without Field-Name
          Duplication
        </h3>
        <p>
          In formats like JSON, an array of 10,000 sub-messages (
          <code>[&#123;"city":"FRA","rack":42&#125;, ...]</code>) repeats the field name strings{' '}
          <code>"city"</code> and <code>"rack"</code> 10,000 times. In OmniBuf, the parent message's{' '}
          <code>Field #0</code> hoists the child schema into <code>children[fieldNum]</code>{' '}
          <strong>once</strong> (or Element 0 of a standalone array carries <code>Field #0</code>),
          and all <code>N</code> elements in the <code>WireSubMsgArr</code> omit{' '}
          <code>Field #0</code> completely:
        </p>
        <pre><code>Parent Message Field #0 (SchemaMeta):
  fields   = &#123; 1: "id", 10: "neighbors" &#125;
  children = &#123;
    10: SchemaMeta &#123;
      type_name: "Neighbor",
      fields: &#123; 1: "peer_asn", 2: "router", 3: "latency_us", 4: "established" &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;

Data Field #10 (WireSubMsgArr, N = 10,000 elements):
  [ElemLen_0][Elem_0 (pure compact tags+values, 0 bytes of repeated field names)]
  [ElemLen_1][Elem_1 (pure compact tags+values, even if optional fields vary)]
  ...
  [ElemLen_9999][Elem_9999]</code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li>
            When <code>DecodeBlind</code> decodes Field <code>#10</code> (<code>WireSubMsgArr</code>
            , <code>WireSubMsg</code>, or a <code>WireMap</code> whose values are{' '}
            <code>WireSubMsg</code>), it passes <code>activeSchema.children[10]</code> down as the
            initial active schema for every child element.
          </li>
          <li>
            If an individual child element also includes its own inline <code>Field #0</code>, its{' '}
            <code>SchemaMeta</code> is merged with the inherited child schema.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 id="sec-8-4">
          8.4 Raw Concatenation (<code>append(msgA, msgB...)</code>) with <code>Field #0</code>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Because <code>Field #0</code> is a standard <code>WireSubMsg</code> (<code>5</code>) whose
          maps use <code>WireMap</code> (<code>9</code>), concatenating two self-describing messages
          (<code>append(msgA, msgB...)</code>) works seamlessly without special framing: when{' '}
          <code>DecodeBlind</code> encounters a second <code>Field #0</code> later in the stream, it
          recursively merges the new <code>SchemaMeta</code> (<code>type_name</code>,{' '}
          <code>fields</code>, and <code>children</code>) into the active <code>SchemaMeta</code>.
        </p>

